WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.858 --> 00:00:05.298
(knocking)

00:00:05.298 --> 00:00:06.381
- [Mark] Who's that?

00:00:06.381 --> 00:00:08.820
- Just wait a minute, yes,
I'll be out in a second!

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:09.903
- [Mark] Just five minutes.

00:00:10.859 --> 00:00:12.000
- [Tori] Ah damn...

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.950
- [Mark] So Tori, so let's start over.

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:15.590
So, where are you from originally?

00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:16.756
- [Tori] I'm from Chicago.

00:00:16.756 --> 00:00:18.687
- [Mark] Chicago. And how
long have you been out here?

00:00:18.687 --> 00:00:22.549
- [Tori] I've been out
here for uh, 20 years.

00:00:22.549 --> 00:00:23.382
- [Mark] 20 years.

00:00:23.382 --> 00:00:24.215
- [Tori] Uh huh.

00:00:24.215 --> 00:00:26.633
- [Mark] And, what's
your drug of choice here?

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:28.373
- Um, heroin.

00:00:28.373 --> 00:00:30.312
- [Mark] Heroin. How long
have you been doing heroin?

00:00:30.312 --> 00:00:32.035
- Um, 12 years.

00:00:32.035 --> 00:00:33.361
- [Mark] 12 years.

00:00:33.361 --> 00:00:35.140
Did you do drugs as a
kid? When you were young?

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:40.140
- Um, I did pot and
methamphetamine, cocaine.

00:00:42.970 --> 00:00:44.420
- [Mark] What age did
you start with drugs?

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:45.253
- Uh, 15.

00:00:46.172 --> 00:00:47.172
- [Mark] 15.

00:00:48.638 --> 00:00:50.288
Who got you started with that?

00:00:50.288 --> 00:00:51.788
- Uh, a boyfriend.

00:00:53.269 --> 00:00:54.590
- [Mark] A boyfriend.

00:00:54.590 --> 00:00:55.423
- [Tori] Yeah.

00:00:55.423 --> 00:00:57.321
- [Mark] Did you have parents,
both parents? One parent?

00:00:57.321 --> 00:00:59.230
- [Tori] Um, I had one parent.

00:00:59.230 --> 00:01:03.770
I had a mother who was an
alcoholic and a drug addict.

00:01:05.271 --> 00:01:06.360
So I would start

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:09.050
every day a drug addict from the get go.

00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:09.883
- [Mark] Got it.

00:01:10.717 --> 00:01:13.840
And what do you do for money now?

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.230
You pick pick up guys sometimes?

00:01:15.230 --> 00:01:17.553
- [Tori] Sometimes I, um, I prostitute.

00:01:19.063 --> 00:01:20.010
- [Mark] It's dangerous out here.

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:22.100
- [Tori] Yeah it is. It's very dangerous.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:24.478
I've almost gotten
killed a couple of times.

00:01:24.478 --> 00:01:25.627
- [Mark] Really?

00:01:25.627 --> 00:01:26.460
- [Tori] Yeah.

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:27.293
- [Mark] How's that?

00:01:27.293 --> 00:01:31.970
- [Tori] Um, I had some guy,
uh, I had been gang raped.

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:36.603
I was pulled into a um,

00:01:39.188 --> 00:01:40.707
a um, stairwell

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:45.530
and was gang raped and left for dead.

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:49.340
Um, I had a guy hit me in
the head with a two by four

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:52.520
and I didn't want to go to the hospital

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:55.210
because I had heroin on me.

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:58.833
So, I just put a bandaid
on, on it and went back out,

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:01.270
did it again.

00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:04.640
You know, it's a bad, it's
just a bad environment.

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:06.880
Dangerous, you never know
what's going to happen.

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:08.740
- [Mark] Yeah. Where do you stay at night?

00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:09.573
Where do you sleep?

00:02:09.573 --> 00:02:11.033
- [Tori] Um, wherever I can.

00:02:15.154 --> 00:02:16.440
- [Mark] Do you have children?

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:17.273
- I did.

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:19.230
- [Mark] You put them

00:02:20.196 --> 00:02:21.029
up for adoption?
- Um, I had,

00:02:21.029 --> 00:02:23.119
my children were taken away from me

00:02:23.119 --> 00:02:27.483
when they were five and seven.

00:02:28.850 --> 00:02:30.300
Because I was a heroin addict

00:02:31.570 --> 00:02:34.120
and then I went to prison
and I couldn't get clean.

00:02:35.190 --> 00:02:36.910
- [Mark] Prison was for what?

00:02:36.910 --> 00:02:39.710
- For a possession and sale of a narcotic

00:02:39.710 --> 00:02:41.077
to an undercover cop.

00:02:41.077 --> 00:02:42.077
- [Mark] Oh.

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:45.338
- If I could take it all back, I would.

00:02:45.338 --> 00:02:47.819
- [Mark] Yeah. What's your biggest regret?

00:02:47.819 --> 00:02:49.268
- Losing my children.

00:02:49.268 --> 00:02:51.209
- [Mark] Losing your kids.

00:02:51.209 --> 00:02:53.198
- Losing my kids.

00:02:53.198 --> 00:02:55.818
- [Mark] Do you ever talk to them at all?

00:02:55.818 --> 00:02:56.651
Never?

00:02:56.651 --> 00:02:57.969
- No.

00:02:57.969 --> 00:03:02.317
No, it's the biggest
regret I've had in my life.

00:03:02.317 --> 00:03:04.017
If I could take it back, I would.

00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:05.653
I'd start all over again.

00:03:09.350 --> 00:03:11.950
The biggest mistake I ever
made was coming out here.

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:15.979
- [Mark] Have you ever been clean?

00:03:15.979 --> 00:03:16.812
- Hmm?

00:03:16.812 --> 00:03:18.067
- [Mark] Have you ever gotten clean?

00:03:18.067 --> 00:03:20.910
- Um, yeah, I was clean
for a little while.

00:03:20.910 --> 00:03:22.477
- [Mark] When you were in prison?

00:03:22.477 --> 00:03:23.865
- When I was in prison,

00:03:23.865 --> 00:03:26.065
and then when I got out
I went to a program,

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:31.390
and then I left the program

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:35.150
and just said fuck it, you know,

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:37.263
why should I stay clean, you know?

00:03:39.670 --> 00:03:42.080
There's no reason for me to
stay clean and watch my kids.

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:43.520
I've lost everything, so

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:48.573
I really didn't care if I
lived or died, you know?

00:03:51.507 --> 00:03:52.340
(sniffs)

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:54.057
- [Mark] Well, thank you
so much for talking to me.

00:03:54.057 --> 00:03:54.890
- Thanks.

00:03:54.890 --> 00:03:57.473
- [Mark] Do you got the camera?

